  "solution": {
    "text": "<blockquote><p>Note: This question is given bonus by JEE council.</p><p>In one rotation 2 divisions of the main scale are crossed. Therefore, the least count of the screw gauge is</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>L</mi><mi>C</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>&#215;</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>5</mn></mrow><mn>100</mn></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>01</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>mm</mi></math></p><p>And the zero error is&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>4</mn><mo>&#215;</mo><mi>L</mi><mi>C</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>04</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>mm</mi></math></p><p>Reading-1</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>R</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mi>MSR</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>LC</mi><mo>&#215;</mo><mi>CSR</mi><mo>-</mo><mfenced><mrow><mi>Zero</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>error</mi></mrow></mfenced></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>=</mo><mfenced><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>+</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>20</mn><mo>-</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>04</mn></mrow></mfenced><mi>mm</mi></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>16</mn><mi>mm</mi></math></p><p>Reading-2</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>R</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mfenced><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>+</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>16</mn><mo>-</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>04</mn></mrow></mfenced><mi>mm</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>12</mn><mi>mm</mi></math></p><p>Therefore, average reading&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>R</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>R</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>R</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>14</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>mm</mi></math></p><p>Average mean error&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mfenced close=\"|\" open=\"|\"><mrow><msub><mi>R</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><mo>-</mo><msub><mi>R</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow></mfenced><mo>+</mo><mfenced close=\"|\" open=\"|\"><mrow><msub><mi>R</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><mo>-</mo><msub><mi>R</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow></mfenced></mrow><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>02</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>mm</mi></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo></math>&nbsp;Diameter&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>d</mi><mo>=</mo><mfenced><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>14</mn><mo>&#177;</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>02</mn></mrow></mfenced><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>mm</mi></math></p><p>Area&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>&#960;</mi><msup><mi>d</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mn>4</mn></mfrac></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#8710;</mo><mi>Area</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>2</mn><mi>&#960;</mi><mi>d</mi></mrow><mn>4</mn></mfrac><mfenced><mrow><mo>&#8710;</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow></mfenced></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#8710;</mo><mi>Area</mi><mo>&#8773;</mo><mi>&#960;</mi><mfenced><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>02</mn></mrow></mfenced></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>Area</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>&#960;</mi><msup><mi>d</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mn>4</mn></mfrac><mo>&#177;</mo><mo>&#8710;</mo><mi>Area</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>&#960;</mi><mfenced><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>14</mn><mo>&#177;</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>02</mn></mrow></mfenced><mo>&#160;</mo><msup><mi>mm</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></math></p></blockquote>"
  }
